Z||000000||shelfran||05-13-2001||09:22 PM||||I have 5 Fieros. My 88 has a bad 2.5 engine. I would like to take the 2.5 out of my 86 but I have been told that the 88 was a special engine..the coil set up is different and the computer and other things won't work.<BR>Can I change the engine and the computer and if so, will the 88 function ok? Or please tell me what I can do if anything to use the 86 engine so I won't have to buy one for the 88. Thanks for your help...Frank Sheldon<P>------------------<BR>Frank Sheldon||||reg||6
Z||000001||Raydar||05-13-2001||10:14 PM||||87s and 88s went to DIS (no distributor) ignition. The entire ECM and engine harness is different. If you change ECMs and engine harness, I don't know what else, if anything, will need to be changed. <BR>For example... The 87 and 88 4 cylinder had the cruise control logic built in to the ECM. All other cars had a separate module. Not sure if there are any other "gotchas" or not. Maybe someone else can help.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
